#: ../guide/commissions.md:1 9cc2b1923eb3444ca2fd4fb6b35e9a09
msgid "Commissions and slippage"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:3 0b6bf192ef0340a69a460e10ce53e9a7
msgid ""
"QTrade ships four `Commission` implementations covering the patterns most"
" strategies need. All live in `qtrade.core.commission` and share the "
"abstract base `Commission`."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:16 149cb340ca8740d78523c0da4162bf95
msgid ""
"Pass an instance to `Backtest(..., commission=...)` or `TradingEnv(..., "
"commission=...)`. `commission=None` is equivalent to `NoCommission()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:20 ae378138f40e4cf5b2a0d4b2bbd54c25
msgid "The interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:22 0195556d9fc54bed8a271a24d18b45da
msgid ""
"`Commission.calculate_commission(order_size: int, fill_price: float) -> "
"float`"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:24 9fa182c2f2924602be8e0234bb47e768
msgid ""
"Returns the commission in account currency for a single fill. The Broker "
"subtracts it from `cash` at fill time. Sign of `order_size` is preserved "
"— use `abs(order_size)` inside if you want symmetric fees on buys and "
"sells."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:29 7eab0e478d214778af61e6854e7ce164
msgid "To roll your own:"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:43 66a6132aa9264c93aa3d6c477b87f773
msgid "Built-in implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:45 b7d01575197644a0b621aaff022cd54f
msgid "NoCommission"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:51 2d0d1704230c40479d9293757637049a
msgid ""
"Returns `0.0` always. The default if you don't pass anything. Use it for "
"clean comparisons against Buy & Hold, or when modeling commission-free "
"brokers."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:55 3b3f5f0724f8483a875f09308fa1f468
msgid "PercentageCommission"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:61 b3519dbea7ee49348f10b015ede3903b
msgid "Charges `abs(order_size) * fill_price * percentage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:63 082f82db95174cbe9373aa0b4da36666
msgid ""
"The standard model for **stocks** (commissions quoted as bps of notional)"
" and **crypto spot** (taker fees are typically 0.05–0.1%)."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:66 de0be0bea8c64ea0ba8df3038630995a
msgid "FixedCommission"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:72 07839273f9b14af4a1d1d269ac0d9300
msgid ""
"Returns a flat fee regardless of size or price. Realistic for **futures**"
" (where the exchange charges per-contract) and for **discount brokers** "
"that quote a flat ticket charge."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:76 6e221c0aa3624645ac005b2219579595
msgid ""
"For futures with multiple commission components (exchange + clearing + "
"broker), sum them up: `FixedCommission(fixed_fee=2.50)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:79 8307916f17aa46369bb0c648a719cdb4
msgid "SlippageCommission"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:85 fe73250a09c54050887e9f3c1cfa88c1
msgid ""
"Mathematically identical to `PercentageCommission`, but the intent is "
"different — this models the *price impact* of crossing the spread, not a "
"venue fee. Use it when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:89 42ed7965fa2a4a9db1091d4f65ca400a
msgid "You want to add slippage **on top of** an explicit commission."
msgstr ""

#: ../guide/commissions.md:90 c86e86351f6e43a089ca12477d998d83
msgid ""
"You want the cost to scale with notional but separate from \"fees\" in "
"reporting."
msgstr ""

